      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Total daily dose:** 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. The FDA-labeled maximum for immediate-release metformin is 2,550 mg/day, which is about double that.\n- **Single dose:** 1700 mg is well above the usual maximum of 1,000 mg per dose. Immediate-release doses are typically 500\u20131,000 mg.\n- **Risk:** Overdosing raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg twice daily\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg** per dose, at a frequency that fits the clinical goal\n\nTell me the dose you intended and I'll enter it. If 1,700 mg three times daily is intentional, tell me the clinical reason and I can enter it with a note, though I'd suggest confirming with pharmacy first."
      }
     ],
